<title>USA: Network Computing settles lawsuits.</title>
<headline>Network Computing settles lawsuits.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNTAIN VIEW, Calif. 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Network Computing Devices Inc Thursday said it reached an agreement-in-principle to settle all pending securities litigation brought against the company last spring.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said it will contribute a total of $1.1 million toward a $12 million settlement cost, covering certain expenses associated with both the federal and California state litigation, which alleged violations of securities laws.</p>
<p>The companys said its cost, which will reduce fourth-quarter net income by about $0.02 a share, will be accounted for as an operating expense.</p>
</text>
